<article class="about-content">
  <header class="section-header">
    <p class="section-kicker">About Live</p>
    <h1>A working notebook, left open.</h1>
    <p>The rest of Anthony Creates shows finished things. Live shows the work while it is still moving.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="about-prose">
    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>The way I make things has changed. I increasingly work like a director: imagining, specifying, prototyping quickly with generative tools, then deciding what is right, wrong or worth keeping.</p>
    <p>The available stories about this moment tend towards hype or doom. I’m more interested in lived practice: what it makes possible, what it costs, and where human judgement now sits.</p>

    <h2>What appears here</h2>
    <p>Things made, lessons worth taking away, work I scrapped, and questions I cannot answer yet. Entries stay short and specific because this is a log, not another place to manufacture essays.</p>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>Makers, developers, designers, hobbyists, and anyone trying to recover a creative practice of their own. The invitation is simple: I’m working this out in the open. Come with me.</p>
  </div>
</article>
